# packages/synth — the AUDIO domain as a real prism package (#63 ⋈ #67).
#
# The first domain broken out of the monolith into `packages/<domain>/`
# (`docs/packages-decomposition.md` §7): synth depends on the native audio crate
# `prism-audio` (its `audio_core()` — Oscillator / LowPass / Vca / Envelope + the
# `Signal` type) and runs `.ys` patches against it.
#
# `audio` is a NATIVE dependency: chrysalis (a fixed binary) cannot link a domain
# crate in-process, so `chrysalis run ys/<patch>.ys` finds this manifest, generates +
# caches a runner that links prism-audio, calls its `prelude::core()`, and colimits it
# in through `resolve_with_natives` — the SAME resolver a `.ys` path dep uses, the
# native Core merely supplied (`docs/packages-decomposition.md` §3). A patch then says
# `from audio import Oscillator` and `:: Signal` (the type rides the colimit). prism-
# audio stays fully chrysalis-free — only its zero-arg `prelude::core()` is touched.
# `sink: 'audio'` declares the OUTPUT boundary (`docs/domain-libraries.md` §5): a
# `chrysalis run ys/<patch>.ys --play` drives the engine to prism-audio's device sink
# (`prelude::run_realtime`) instead of rendering offline JSON. `'audio'` names the
# native dependency whose crate provides the sink.
def package = {
  name: 'synth',
  version: '0.1.0',
  dependencies: { audio: { native: '../../crates/prism-audio' } },
  sink: 'audio',
}
